      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: use AXUIElementCopyActionNames for supportedActions()",
        "body": "## Problem\n`supportedActions()` reads the `AXActionNames` attribute via `AXUIElementCopyAttributeValue`. For SwiftUI apps this returns nothing, so `isActionSupported(\"AXPress\")` is always false and every `performAction` fails with `Available actions: []`.\n\n## Fix\nQuery the dedicated `AXUIElementCopyActionNames` API first, keeping the attribute read as a fallback.\n\n## Verification\nReproduced against a SwiftUI app (AXPress on a plain `Button`): before the fix the action was rejected with an empty action list; after the fix the press succeeds. Full test suite still green (51 tests).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "branch": "fix/action-names-api",
